Hi Kevin,

Sorry about the lost history — that's not expected behavior. Logging this
as NOVA-59: wifi credentials/state not surviving an unclean power loss on
0.3.8.

Router logs would help a lot, especially the DHCP lease renewal timestamps
around the outage. You can attach them to this thread.

In the meantime, two things that might reduce the chance of it recurring:
1. Set a static DHCP reservation for the widget's MAC in your router if
   possible — some of our other reports correlate with a *changed* IP after
   reconnect, not just a dropped connection.
2. Avoid factory-resetting next time if it happens again — try holding the
   side button for 3 seconds first (soft wifi-only reset), which keeps
   sensor history intact.

Sam is looping in Jonah on the firmware side since this sounds like it could
be the same state-corruption class of bug as MESH-118, just a different
subsystem (wifi supplicant state vs. relay radio).

Thanks for your patience — batch 4 feedback like this is exactly what the
beta is for.

— Aurora Labs Support
